# XCU unset
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/unset.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.unset.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/unset each variable or function definition
class      required
says       unset name and unset -v name remove a variable (it ends up unset,
           not empty); several names may be given.
test       t/001-variables.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall unset the function definition
class      required
says       unset -f name removes a function, so the name is then not found
           (status 127), and leaves a variable of the same name alone; unset
           -v leaves the function alone.
test       t/002-functions.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/<i>name</i> refers to a variable
class      required
says       Without -f or -v, unset treats the name as a variable: the
           variable goes and a function of the same name stays.
test       t/003-no-option.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall not be considered an error
class      required
says       Unsetting a name that is not set is not an error: status zero and
           the shell goes on.
test       t/004-not-set-ok.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/could not be unset
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/Read-only variables cannot be unset
class      required
says       A read-only variable cannot be unset: unset returns non-zero (the
           shell may exit) and the value stays.
test       t/005-readonly.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/remove it from
class      required
since      2024
says       Unsetting an exported variable removes it from the environment of
           later utilities, and a later assignment does not bring it back.
test       t/006-environment.sh

assertion  XCU.unset.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/special built-in shall support XBD
class      required
says       unset accepts "--" as the end of options.
test       t/007-double-hyphen.sh
